Package: stagelife
Type: Package
Title: Random Number Generation and Inferences for Two-Stage Life-Testing Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Vikas Kumar", "Sharma", email = "vksharma@bhu.ac.in", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides random number generation, estimation, and hypothesis
    testing for two-stage life-testing experiments in which units begin on
    a baseline stress and, at a fixed or random change point, some or all
    surviving units move to an elevated stress ("stage life testing"),
    following the cumulative-exposure model of Laumen and Cramer (2019),
    "Stage life testing", <doi:10.1002/nav.21874>. Twelve baseline lifetime
    distributions are supplied (Weibull, Power Lindley, Exponentiated Lindley,
    Exponentiated Exponential, Marshall-Olkin Exponential, Lomax,
    Exponentiated Teissier, Log-Logistic, Chen, Log-normal, Gamma, and Power
    Muth/Power Teissier) together with three parameter-sharing cases
    ('common', 'shape1', 'shape11'). The package implements data simulation
    under both the fixed-proportion 'typeP' and fixed-count 'typeM' rules
    and the simple-step-stress special case, maximum likelihood estimation
    with a Nelder-Mead/BFGS hybrid optimiser, asymptotic (Wald) and
    non-parametric/parametric bootstrap confidence
    intervals (including log-scale variants that guarantee a positive
    interval), a stage-1-observation planning probability, Kolmogorov-Smirnov
    goodness-of-fit testing with a parametric-bootstrap correction for
    estimated parameters, likelihood-ratio and information criteria for
    nested/non-nested model comparison, and diagnostic plots (fitted
    CDF/survival, P-P, Q-Q).
